<programme start="20261114170000 +0000" stop="20261114203000 +0000" channel="FS1 🇺🇸"><title lang="en">College Football</title><sub-title lang="en">Wisconsin at Maryland</sub-title><desc lang="en">The Badgers (6-3, 4-2 Big Ten) try to exact revenge from the Terrapins (3-6, 1-5). Maryland won for the first time in five tries against Wisconsin, 27-10 in 2025. Maryland snapped a six-game slide with a 34-29 triumph over Purdue last week.</desc><category lang="en">Sports</category><category lang="en">Football</category><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p191261_b_v12_ak.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261114203000 +0000" stop="20261115000000 +0000" channel="FS1 🇺🇸"><title lang="en">College Football</title><sub-title lang="en">Michigan at Oregon</sub-title><desc lang="en">The Michigan Wolverines (5-4) visit the No. 16 Oregon Ducks (6-3) for a Big Ten matchup at Autzen Stadium. Michigan fell to Michigan State 15-6 and relies on Bryce Underwood, while Oregon seek to make it three straight after beating Ohio State 41-28.</desc><category lang="en">Sports</category><category lang="en">Football</category><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p191261_b_v12_ak.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261115000000 +0000" stop="20261115030000 +0000" channel="FS1 🇺🇸"><title lang="en">College Football</title><sub-title lang="en">Minnesota at Penn State</sub-title><desc lang="en">The Penn State Nittany Lions (5-4, 2-4 Big Ten) host the Minnesota Golden Gophers (5-4, 3-3 Big Ten) at Beaver Stadium in University Park. Drake Lindsey leads Minnesota with 11 touchdowns, while Rocco Becht leads Penn State with 15 touchdowns.</desc><category lang="en">Sports</category><category lang="en">Football</category><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p191261_b_v12_ak.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261115030000 +0000" stop="20261115063000 +0000" channel="FS1 🇺🇸"><title lang="en">College Football</title><sub-title lang="en">Wyoming at Texas-El Paso</sub-title><desc lang="en">The UTEP Miners (1-8, 0-5 Mountain West) host the Wyoming Cowboys (6-3, 5-1 Mountain West) at the Sun Bowl in El Paso. Wyoming aims for a five-game win streak behind Tyler Hughes, while UTEP hopes to break a seven-game losing streak.</desc><category lang="en">Sports</category><category lang="en">Football</category><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p191261_b_v12_ak.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261115063000 +0000" stop="20261115093000 +0000" channel="FS1 🇺🇸"><title lang="en">College Football</title><sub-title lang="en">Northwestern at Ohio State</sub-title><desc lang="en">The No. 20 Ohio State Buckeyes (6-3, 4-2 Big Ten) host the Northwestern Wildcats (6-3, 3-3 Big Ten) at Ohio Stadium. Both teams aim to break a two-game skid. Northwestern relies on Aidan Chiles, while Ohio State looks to Julian Sayin.</desc><category lang="en">Sports</category><category lang="en">Football</category><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p191261_b_v12_ak.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261115093000 +0000" stop="20261115123000 +0000" channel="FS1 🇺🇸"><title lang="en">College Football</title><sub-title lang="en">Utah at Arizona</sub-title><desc lang="en">The No. 2 Utes (9-0, 6-0 Big 12) seek their first 10-0 start since 2008 as they visit the No. 23 Wildcats (7-2, 4-2). Utah comes off a 28-20 triumph over rival BYU. Arizona has won seven straight at home following a 29-28 victory over TCU last week.</desc><category lang="en">Sports</category><category lang="en">Football</category><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p191261_b_v12_ak.jpg"/></programme>
